tion monitoring summary.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 13, "week": 3, "level": "Intermediate", "title": "VLOOKUP & Exact Matching", "tool": "Google Sheets", "concepts": "Lookup keys, exact match and why approximate matching can be dangerous.", "objectives": ["Use VLOOKUP with FALSE", "Choose a reliable key", "Identify missing matches"], "practical": "Bring county/program fields from a master table into visit records.", "ai_use": "Ask AI to explain what each argument in your VLOOKUP means using your formula.", "exercise": "Enrich transaction data from a master list.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 14, "week": 3, "level": "Intermediate", "title": "XLOOKUP & IFERROR", "tool": "Google Sheets", "concepts": "More flexible lookups and transparent handling of missing keys.", "objectives": ["Use XLOOKUP", "Handle missing records visibly", "Compare lookup approaches"], "practical": "Replace a VLOOKUP-based solution with XLOOKUP and create an unmatched-record exception count.", "ai_use": "Ask AI to compare VLOOKUP and XLOOKUP, then verify its claims against Google Sheets behavior.", "exercise": "Create resilient lookup logic.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 15, "week": 3, "level": "Intermediate", "title": "Cross-Sheet Reconciliation", "tool": "Google Sheets", "concepts": "Matching two sources and explaining differences.", "objectives": ["Build match status", "Create exception lists", "Use control totals"], "practical": "Reconcile registration and attendance sheets and produce two exception tables.", "ai_use": "Ask AI for questions an auditor would ask about your reconciliation.", "exercise": "Reconcile registration vs attendance.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 16, "week": 4, "level": "Intermediate", "title": "Pivot Tables", "tool": "Google Sheets", "concepts": "Fast grouped summaries and validation of grand totals.", "objectives": ["Create a Pivot Table", "Choose rows/columns/values", "Validate grand totals"], "practical": "Summarize actuals by county and activity, then compare to source totals.", "ai_use": "Ask AI to suggest a pivot layout for a stated question; build and verify it yourself.", "exercise": "Create operational Pivot Tables.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 17, "week": 4, "level": "Intermediate", "title": "Pivot Charts, Slicers & Interactive Views", "tool": "Google Sheets", "concepts": "Turning grouped summaries into interactive analysis.", "objectives": ["Create a Pivot Chart", "Use slicers/filters", "Avoid misleading chart choices"], "practical": "Create a management view by county and officer with an interactive filter.", "ai_use": "Ask AI to critique your chart choice and suggest a clearer alternative if needed.", "exercise": "Build an interactive operations view.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 18, "week": 4, "level": "Intermediate", "title": "Data Quality Audit", "tool": "Google Sheets", "concepts": "Systematic issue counts: missingness, duplicates, invalid ranges and unmatched keys.", "objectives": ["Profile data quality", "Build issue flags", "Create an exception table"], "practical": "Create a QA sheet with issue counts and row-level flags.", "ai_use": "Ask AI to review your QA checklist for missing control types.", "exercise": "Audit a messy operational dataset.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 19, "week": 4, "level": "Intermediate", "title": "KPI Design & Business Questions", "tool": "Google Sheets", "concepts": "Turning vague management questions into measurable metrics.", "objectives": ["Define numerator/denominator", "Choose period and grain", "Document KPI assumptions"], "practical": "Design five KPIs from a program brief, then implement them in a summary sheet.", "ai_use": "Ask AI to challenge each KPI definition for ambiguity or unintended incentives.", "exercise": "Create a KPI definition and calculation sheet.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 20, "week": 4, "level": "Intermediate", "title": "Intermediate Capstone", "tool": "Google Sheets", "concepts": "Multi-sheet analysis with lookups, pivots, QA and management summary.", "objectives": ["Combine multiple sheets", "Produce traceable KPIs", "Create exceptions and visuals"], "practical": "Build a two-source monitoring report with a management page and QA page.", "ai_use": "Use AI only after your first version; ask it to audit logic, not create the whole solution.", "exercise": "Intermediate capstone: multi-sheet monitoring system.", "capstone": true}, {"day": 21, "week": 5, "level": "Advanced", "title": "SQL SELECT, WHERE & ORDER BY", "tool": "SQL", "concepts": "Querying rows and columns from structured data.", "objectives": ["Write SELECT queries", "Filter with WHERE", "Sort results"], "practical": "Load the exercise CSV into SQLite/DB tool and answer six business questions.", "ai_use": "Ask AI to explain an SQL error message and give a hint, not a finished answer.", "exercise": "Query customer/program transactions.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 22, "week": 5, "level": "Advanced", "title": "SQL Aggregation & GROUP BY", "tool": "SQL", "concepts": "COUNT, SUM, AVG and grouped business summaries.", "objectives": ["Aggregate correctly", "Group by dimensions", "Use HAVING"], "practical": "Calculate totals and averages by county/program and filter grouped results.", "ai_use": "Ask AI to test whether your GROUP BY answers the intended business question.", "exercise": "Create grouped SQL summaries.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 23, "week": 5, "level": "Advanced", "title": "SQL JOINs", "tool": "SQL", "concepts": "Combining normalized tables using keys.", "objectives": ["Use INNER/LEFT JOIN", "Recognize one-to-many relationships", "Detect unmatched keys"], "practical": "Join people, activities and reference tables and produce an unmatched-key report.", "ai_use": "Ask AI to draw the join logic in words before you run it, then compare with actual results.", "exercise": "Build joined analytical datasets.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 24, "week": 5, "level": "Advanced", "title": "SQL CTEs & Window Functions", "tool": "SQL", "concepts": "Readable multi-step queries, ranking and cumulative calculations.", "objectives": ["Use WITH/CTE", "Apply ROW_NUMBER/RANK", "Create running totals"], "practical": "Rank performers within county and compute cumulative monthly actuals.", "ai_use": "Ask AI to explain the difference between GROUP BY and window functions with a fresh example.", "exercise": "Create ranking and running-total queries.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 25, "week": 5, "level": "Advanced", "title": "Power Query: Import & Transform", "tool": "Power BI / Power Query", "concepts": "Repeatable data ingestion and transformation.", "objectives": ["Import data", "Change types", "Remove/replace errors", "Document transformation steps"], "practical": "Import two exercise tables, clean types/text and create a reproducible transformation pipeline.", "ai_use": "Ask AI to explain a Power Query step or error; verify against the Applied Steps pane.", "exercise": "Build a repeatable Power Query cleaning pipeline.", "capstone": false}, {"day